    "explanation": "qlib's real Rank uses pandas' average-rank method with pct=True, normalizing by N: a fully-tied window's every element ties for ranks 1..N, whose average is (N+1)/2, so pct = (N+1)/(2N). ARGUS fixes a fully-tied window at exactly 0.5 for every N by design (its own code comment: 'neither high nor low in its own distribution'). The two conventions converge only as N -> inf."
